#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105596 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "b3be2b13-b455-5dde-accf-259c075e1e1f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4350" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-4,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,-2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,0,3 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)+4(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))+2(0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-6+4-4 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV = |-6| = 6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105597 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/id #uuid "c6f2dacc-11b0-5689-97d9-e1869c64aae1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4351" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle k,2,1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -2,-1,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,1,2 \\rangle$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(-1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-2(-2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1)+(-2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-3k+6-3 \\\\  & =-3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -3k+3 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105598 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/id #uuid "4deee6cc-69e4-5da4-9c78-57bf6c988500" :question/math-academy-id "e-4352" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD},$ given the points $A(3,-1,2),$ $B(2,1,1),$ $C(-1,2,1),$ and $D(4,4,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+4j+2k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(3\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-1))-2((-4)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1))-((-4)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-5-2+23 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|16|=16.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262892 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f850623-1cf0-5b7f-b020-c07acfebbd8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260983} {:answer/id #uuid "9baefb07-c1d1-5b54-860e-b68104387cb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261224} {:answer/id #uuid "b255695f-5469-5e72-bef9-0b28e1845792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261451} {:answer/id #uuid "e4a3d805-1618-5717-aa44-a03a5852416b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261886} {:answer/id #uuid "e4d4c9d9-60a8-5e94-b5ef-2dd4a95c4889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4a3d805-1618-5717-aa44-a03a5852416b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261886} :answer-field/id #uuid "40927668-f3a3-5ce4-80d8-9ec8828fb9da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59779a24-408f-5832-999c-31c9f5625f84" :question/math-academy-id "q-128421" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $p=⟨2,2,3⟩,$ $q=⟨4,2,-1⟩,$ and $r=⟨-5,0,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot 3-0\\cdot (-1))-2(4\\cdot 3-(-5)\\cdot (-1))+3(4\\cdot 0-(-5)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =12-14+30 \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|28|=28.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12a3758c-f60c-5dae-92fa-afedc78160ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458653} {:answer/id #uuid "1c111100-d619-5b93-b482-b6ec810b8df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458679} {:answer/id #uuid "3f06b20c-1420-5939-96cc-465d37b4df29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458746} {:answer/id #uuid "856f42a7-be02-543a-b498-4b18fecdaca0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458860} {:answer/id #uuid "96678253-6e22-571e-98ff-a64d81bbbdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96678253-6e22-571e-98ff-a64d81bbbdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458889} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef466f3-b445-5f7c-961a-8d3a58c07b04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459092}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2eedb023-f05d-5365-a7fb-580375aea9cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-128442" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $p=⟨5,-2,2⟩,$ $q=⟨3,k,1⟩,$ and $r=⟨-8,3,-4⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & k & 1 \\\\ -8 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -8 & -4\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ -8 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5(k\\cdot (-4)-3\\cdot 1)+2(3\\cdot (-4)-(-8)\\cdot 1)+2(3\\cdot 3-(-8)\\cdot k) \\\\  & =-20k-15-8+18+16k \\\\  & =-4k-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ -4k-5 & =0 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{5}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459264 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2edcbb95-8455-53f6-ab2b-7ee4b7636b26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{48}{89}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458720} {:answer/id #uuid "952a2910-c243-5005-89e0-a85dc85a351b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458888} {:answer/id #uuid "b7055a4c-b19c-53cc-bd20-a53224e1ac3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{48}{89}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458958} {:answer/id #uuid "d351447b-72b1-5263-b183-d42c3b9c1db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458996} {:answer/id #uuid "fb3fdd87-8f4b-5ed1-abd8-52ae4ff972fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb3fdd87-8f4b-5ed1-abd8-52ae4ff972fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459073} :answer-field/id #uuid "20c78fd9-b62d-5bc1-a554-90d9058aa00b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459098}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a1fc629c-e7ef-51c7-b925-1dba79c32351" :question/math-academy-id "q-128457" :question/problem "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨9,9,-2⟩,$ $q=⟨5,6,0⟩,$ and $r=⟨4,t,t⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}9 & 9 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 4 & t & t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =9\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ t & t\\end{aligned}|-9\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & t\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =9(6\\cdot t-t\\cdot 0)-9(5\\cdot t-4\\cdot 0)-2(5\\cdot t-4\\cdot 6) \\\\  & =54t-45t-10t+48 \\\\  & =48-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 48-t & =0 \\\\ t & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=48.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459280 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5216c374-a69c-5443-8bee-9f1ddd0f5f48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458774} {:answer/id #uuid "6335e762-2245-5418-bb75-3a1949475345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458799} {:answer/id #uuid "e1689190-63f6-546f-8a11-0c26f5505614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459019} {:answer/id #uuid "e266aadb-6f3e-5cb3-bdf0-fbd14964466f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459022} {:answer/id #uuid "f5efc6f5-034d-561c-9f26-ee84c3ed3263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e266aadb-6f3e-5cb3-bdf0-fbd14964466f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459022} :answer-field/id #uuid "86bdb8ca-60d6-5ea6-b69c-33f89749693f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459144}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bf74fac3-a1be-5590-922d-8474c31e9763" :question/math-academy-id "q-128471" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(0,9,4),$ $B(3,8,2),$ $C(2,9,1),$ and $D(-1,7,7).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+8j+2k)-(9j+4k) \\\\  & =3i-j-2k \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(2i+9j+k)-(9j+4k) \\\\  & =2i-3k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(-i+7j+7k)-(9j+4k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(0\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot (-3))+(2\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot (-3))-2(2\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-18+3+8 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-7|=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459239 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4745fa01-7267-5d7d-80a7-da776c08b11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458758} {:answer/id #uuid "6a6770d3-5bd6-55b6-b578-032b42984508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458815} {:answer/id #uuid "87767553-4117-55d5-ab34-eebfa1e2b999" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458866} {:answer/id #uuid "9b91be34-01c4-5335-b541-f723bc434b99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458902} {:answer/id #uuid "9e493727-fb30-528b-be73-42746650771c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4745fa01-7267-5d7d-80a7-da776c08b11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458758} :answer-field/id #uuid "cffe9ad2-0939-5976-9d7b-05a76872555a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5208cfc4-b7ed-5787-b174-631ca841e3f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-128486" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(8,0,5),$ $B(8,-3,3),$ $C(5,2,5),$ and $D(7,-1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(8i-3j+3k)-(8i+5k) \\\\  & =-3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,-3,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(5i+2j+5k)-(8i+5k) \\\\  & =-3i+2j \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(7i-j+4k)-(8i+5k) \\\\  & =-i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+3((-3)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 0)-2((-3)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =9-10 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-1|=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459308 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097251b1-26d6-5cd9-bf4d-87268a9fc820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458633} {:answer/id #uuid "1b54582f-21c1-5dbb-96a1-354563e5dd55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458675} {:answer/id #uuid "2cada373-4b44-51da-8246-3a0563bdb1ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{125}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458715} {:answer/id #uuid "746350b5-80dc-5a7c-a6bb-5b2627a66dd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{125}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458833} {:answer/id #uuid "f5f276ab-f70a-50eb-8278-8d17070d15a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "746350b5-80dc-5a7c-a6bb-5b2627a66dd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{125}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458833} :answer-field/id #uuid "79226ded-2796-54ed-af2f-9b7e026caf73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa437fb9-bfe8-5dbc-864c-e499156b0343" :question/math-academy-id "q-18261" :question/problem "Find $x$ given that the vectors $a=⟨12,-2x,1⟩$ , $b=⟨1,5,-2⟩$ and $c=⟨-9,4,8⟩$  are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}12 & -2x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =12\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}|-(-2x)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 8\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =12(5\\cdot 8-4\\cdot (-2))+2x(1\\cdot 8-(-9)\\cdot (-2))+(1\\cdot 4-5\\cdot (-9)) \\\\  & =576-20x+49 \\\\  & =625-20x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 625-20x & =0 \\\\ 20x & =625 \\\\ x & =\\frac{125}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $x=\\frac{125}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030d4dbf-31a4-5c0b-ac81-fba854373f33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458621} {:answer/id #uuid "73574c6b-9bf8-53da-8eb4-4206538d870d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458830} {:answer/id #uuid "9f870293-8ab2-51ce-aeed-f745f0ba194c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458911} {:answer/id #uuid "beb8454a-c986-5919-9b86-28dfc102e89c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458970} {:answer/id #uuid "e4c4fd6b-08ec-58ae-80a4-d8e5d351c013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4c4fd6b-08ec-58ae-80a4-d8e5d351c013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459025} :answer-field/id #uuid "70ec86a9-e96a-54b6-bdab-92b2a2a8c0ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f94fb95c-1aca-535d-ab25-0d9749d43fb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-18262" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $p=⟨0,1,-1⟩$, $q=⟨-2,3,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-1,4,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-((-2)\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 1)-((-2)\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =5+5 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|10|=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4b54cc7-eae3-5d57-91d2-3a0fea3a1c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "152" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458919} {:answer/id #uuid "b303e1bb-f85e-5fac-8e2e-0800f3853ee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "161" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458950} {:answer/id #uuid "bf8935c4-627d-5119-a734-99dcd8c66458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "153" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458972} {:answer/id #uuid "e0b30beb-61fb-5067-98b9-8e9d6b43d7f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-134" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459017} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7b07bc-b3d2-5466-b600-1f239c376357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{155}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf8935c4-627d-5119-a734-99dcd8c66458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "153" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458972} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9a5041e-ac12-543b-a288-c49e2bf1590e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "da5d7cb9-5c27-5b41-96e4-8767d3252a54" :question/math-academy-id "q-20144" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(3,-2,2)$, $B(4,3,2)$, $C(1,3,5)$, $D(2,4,-6).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i+3j+2k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+3j+5k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =-2i+5j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-2,5,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+4j-6k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+6j-8k \\\\  & =⟨-1,6,-8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 6 & -8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -8\\end{aligned}|-5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -8\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(5\\cdot (-8)-6\\cdot 3)-5((-2)\\cdot (-8)-(-1)\\cdot 3)+0 \\\\  & =-58-95 \\\\  & =-153.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-153|=153.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459217 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "255146d3-f1ae-58a0-bbc3-4ee1dacf192e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "255146d3-f1ae-58a0-bbc3-4ee1dacf192e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458703} :answer-field/id #uuid "8056469f-7633-5bdb-aee2-dd21051fcade" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "250fb4d2-3fa7-5b45-a7da-bbdf1bb4b98b" :question/math-academy-id "q-280323" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,1,1),$ $B(2,3,4),$ $C(-1,2,0),$ and $D(3,0,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+3j+4k)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =i+2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =-2i+j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i+5k)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =2i-j+4k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot (-1))-2((-2)\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot 2)+3((-2)\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =1(4-1)-2(-8+2)+3(2-2) \\\\  & =3+12+0 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|15|=15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91e13210-c3e8-5a66-8d62-7a2167a2e669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91e13210-c3e8-5a66-8d62-7a2167a2e669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458883} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3dc73c2-9dbe-5591-bf8d-362e058d27f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c8774189-53cd-55b6-bea0-346937f16124" :question/math-academy-id "q-280710" :question/problem "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $a=⟨4,0,2⟩$, $b=⟨1,3,0⟩$, and $c=⟨0,2,5⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(3\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 2)+0+2(1\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =60+0+4 \\\\  & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|64|=64.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295169 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "153692ac-17dc-5340-8ab8-c764df7ca660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "153692ac-17dc-5340-8ab8-c764df7ca660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293019} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b34c4d0-3f40-5fab-a961-3f1c1324f59d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "61f3e6a0-31a0-537c-a9de-e6c7ae59826e" :question/math-academy-id "q-280722" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨1,3,0⟩$, $b=⟨0,4,2⟩$, and $c=⟨2,k,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\na\\cdot (b\\times c)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k & 5\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ k & 5\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 5-2\\cdot k)-3(0\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 2)=(20-2k)+12 \\\\  & =32-2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 32-2k & =0 \\\\ -2k & =-32 \\\\ k & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379355 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8d6275c-2c2f-59ab-b7b4-5b1eda58e833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379357} {:answer/id #uuid "b445dedd-49e6-575a-8fa2-7a20bed64a1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b445dedd-49e6-575a-8fa2-7a20bed64a1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458954} :answer-field/id #uuid "10207b0f-c379-5c84-8c28-c24da6e3a13b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfbdee37-0e15-5189-bc70-8dfc3870c722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379359} {:answer/id #uuid "76db5a28-a5e0-562a-b8e3-32e309b442e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76db5a28-a5e0-562a-b8e3-32e309b442e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458838} :answer-field/id #uuid "62836b52-5826-5320-94c6-63c604cf8b0d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe6d904a-8846-5cf7-a75e-99f480622386" :question/math-academy-id "q-280772" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $x=⟨{k}^{2},-2,5⟩$, $y=⟨1,3,4⟩$, and $z=⟨0,-1,2⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n**In ascending order:** $\\,$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}\n$\\,$\nand\n$\\,$\n$k=${{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2} & -2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={k}^{2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={k}^{2}(3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot (-1))+2(1\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 0)+5(1\\cdot -1-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & ={k}^{2}(6+4)+2(2)+5(-1) \\\\  & =10{k}^{2}+4-5 \\\\  & =10{k}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =0 \\\\ 10{k}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ 10{k}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ k & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if \n$k=-\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{10}}$ or $k=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{10}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "993b3b03-f3d6-5055-808b-fcb8eae46a03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "993b3b03-f3d6-5055-808b-fcb8eae46a03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458894} :answer-field/id #uuid "09c71cbe-d318-5b84-9c56-0344d5f8371b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1a41586e-8435-5507-a7ef-851c0478678b" :question/math-academy-id "q-281027" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(3,1,2),$ $B(0,5,0),$ $C(3,3,1),$ and $D(1,4,2).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(5j)-(3i+1j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+4j-2k \\\\  & =⟨-3,4,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+3j+1k)-(3i+1j+2k) \\\\  & =2j-1k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(1i+4j+2k)-(3i+1j+2k) \\\\  & =-2i+3j \\\\  & =⟨-2,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(2\\cdot 0-(-1)(3))-4(0\\cdot 0-(-1)(-2))+(-2)(0\\cdot 3-2\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-3(3)-4(-2)-2(4) \\\\  & =-9-8+8 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-9|=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459275 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a4c55ab-5c11-591a-ae51-5858bb8b481e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458638} {:answer/id #uuid "14ba0b46-50bc-55aa-8afd-659259db34e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458662} {:answer/id #uuid "742d97ab-9f7c-5567-8851-19c88e61766c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458832} {:answer/id #uuid "89d83a6d-9b11-560d-9b1f-652553495081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458871} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb99b8e-8f53-513e-9d9d-5f7e24a3cbd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdb99b8e-8f53-513e-9d9d-5f7e24a3cbd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459079} :answer-field/id #uuid "2515701c-5375-5820-8a2d-3a0891924183" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459100}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b387009d-e229-5370-99a6-bec87fcc7e69" :question/math-academy-id "q-42053" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨1,2,4⟩$, $b=⟨3,5,-7⟩$ and $c=⟨1,0,2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-7))-2(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-7))+4(3\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =10-26-20 \\\\  & =-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|-36|=36.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24585c6e-39f5-5de1-bfc1-0173664ae181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458701} {:answer/id #uuid "5b8513cd-ab93-5f19-bf47-89063e84a0d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "76" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458780} {:answer/id #uuid "8e663096-bc65-50c5-bf7a-24f45672c008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458875} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba547f4-f014-5db1-b028-89db94f43cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458903} {:answer/id #uuid "b050aca3-3130-5bde-8b37-6ba509d74c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ba547f4-f014-5db1-b028-89db94f43cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458903} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe68fa49-351f-5bc9-8911-9305bb6e6c31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8fcc06ee-9e96-5a19-8006-dabebc81e1fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-42055" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-1,2,5⟩$, $b=⟨1,-4,2⟩$ and $c=⟨0,5,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-((-4)\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 2)-2(1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 2)+5(1\\cdot 5-0\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =14-2+25 \\\\  & =37\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|37|=37.\n$$"}]}
